              "26 U.S.C. § 41(d)(1)(B)(i); 26 CFR § 1.41-4(a)(3)(ii), § 1.41-4(a)(4)",
              "The research must be undertaken for the purpose of discovering information that is technological in nature, meaning the evaluative process fundamentally relies on the principles of the physical or biological sciences, engineering, or computer science. Under Treasury Decision (TD) 9104 and 26 CFR § 1.41-4(a)(3)(ii), the taxpayer may employ existing technologies and scientific principles and is not required to expand or refine the common knowledge of skilled professionals in the field, nor is the activity required to succeed in developing the intended business component. Research in the <a href=\"/us/glossary/social-sciences-exclusion\">social sciences</a>, arts, humanities, economics, market research, and routine data processing are statutorily excluded."
