        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "<em>Little Sandy Coal</em> (2023) penalized whole-project claiming without activity-level records; <em>Meyer, Borgman & Johnson</em> (2024) denied a structural engineering firm's credits because its contracts did not make payment contingent on research success; and <em>Smith</em> (2026) confirmed that copyright transfers and milestone billing can eliminate or limit an architectural firm's credit. Mandatory Section G reporting for tax years beginning after 2025 and the reinstated <a href=\"/us/faq/does-rd-tax-credit-reduce-tax-basis-section-280c\">§280C(c) coordination rule</a> add a compliance and valuation layer that every consultant must now handle."
