        "text": "<strong>Analysis.</strong> The U.S. independence rules bear directly on this comparison. When the Big 4 firm is also the client's auditor and the client is subject to PCAOB rules (an issuer or other audit client of a registered firm), the firm cannot take the R&D study on a <a href=\"/us/faq/standard-rd-tax-credit-contingency-fee\">contingent (percentage-of-credit) fee</a>, and the engagement needs audit-committee pre-approval after the Rule 3524 disclosures. This cuts both ways. For a private company that is not subject to PCAOB rules, AICPA independence rules apply instead; those rules were not reviewed for this report."
