        "text": "<strong>Clarification.</strong> Both cases were audit-quality enforcement actions outside the United States. Neither found that conflicts arising from consulting or tax work caused the failures. They show regulatory concern about objectivity in general. They are not evidence about the quality of U.S. R&D tax credit claims prepared by either type of provider."
