          "<strong>Qualified.</strong> Audit is about a third of Big 4 revenue at all four firms, not a fifth. The Wirecard and Carillion cases were non-U.S. audit-quality failures, not findings about tax-credit conflicts. Post-2025 changes to §§ 41(d)(1)(A), 174A and 280C(c) make coordination with the client's tax return more important, which can favor a provider that also prepares the return.",
          "<strong>Weak evidence.</strong> The headline figures on time burden, fees and missed savings come from vendor or marketing content. Two case figures belong to a general CPA firm or include non-R&D credits, and one fee range is from the UK."
