        "text": "In the IRS <em>Audit Guidelines on the Application of the Process of Experimentation for All Software</em>, examiners classify software development activities into three audit risk tiers: High Risk (activities that usually fail to constitute qualified research under IRC § 41(d)), Moderate Risk (activities that often fail), and Low Risk (activities that rarely fail). Seven specific High-Risk categories identified by the IRS directly govern—and frequently disqualify—common digital agency technical workflows."
