        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "In <strong>Section G (Business Component Information, Columns 49(a)–56)</strong>, taxpayers must report granular QRE breakdowns disaggregated by individual business component. Completing Section G is optional for taxable years beginning before 2026—unless the taxpayer is claiming an initial or increased research credit on an amended return, in which case completing Section G and describing the information sought to be discovered in Column 49(f) is mandatory to constitute a <a href=\"/us/faq/irs-guidance-rd-tax-credit-refund-claims\">valid administrative refund claim</a>—and becomes <strong>mandatory for taxable years beginning after 2025</strong>. Even for taxable years beginning after 2025, a digital marketing agency is exempt from completing Section G if it satisfies one of two statutory exceptions: first, the <strong>Payroll Tax Credit Exception</strong>, where the agency is a Qualified Small Business (QSB) under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41h-payroll-tax-credit-qualified-small-businesses\">IRC § 41(h)(3)</a> electing to apply up to $500,000 of its research credit against the employer portion of Social Security payroll taxes; or second, the <strong>De Minimis QRE / Gross Receipts Exception</strong>, where the agency reports $1.5 million or less in total QREs (determined at the controlled group level on Line 48) <em>and</em> has $50 million or less in average annual gross receipts for the three preceding taxable years under IRC § 448(c)(3), provided the credit is claimed on a timely filed original return."
