        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Conversely, several state jurisdictions have enacted transferable tax credit programs that explicitly permit businesses to sell unused state R&D tax credits to unrelated, profitable corporate taxpayers in exchange for cash. Rather than <a href=\"/us/faq/rd-tax-credit-carryforward-rules\">carrying forward unused tax credits</a> for up to 20 years at the federal level (under IRC § 39(a)(1)) or 15 years under applicable state statutes while waiting to achieve profitability, qualifying businesses in these state jurisdictions can monetize their deferred state tax assets on secondary markets, typically realizing between $0.85 and $0.95 per $1.00 of verified credit face value (reflecting a 5% to 20% secondary market and brokerage discount range, with $0.90 per $1.00 serving as the standard analytical baseline)."
