        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "<strong>Analysis:</strong> When companies compare R&D tax advisors, the advisor's competence and independence decide whether the company can rely on that advisor's advice if a penalty is proposed. An advisor whose fee depends on the size of the credit, or who also sells the product being recommended, may be treated as conflicted, and that weakens the reliance defense."
