        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "For a specialized R&D tax advisory firm, dismantling this inertia requires a synchronized operational and financial strategy rather than standalone fee discounting. First, by deploying proprietary AI automation (TaxTrex) and <a href=\"/us/faq/rd-tax-credit-advisors-with-audit-defense\">structured audit defense systems</a> (creditARMOR), the incoming advisor reduces the internal labor cost of ingesting and reconciling complex multi-year tax data, making it economically feasible to absorb 100% of the client's setup and transition costs. Second, by pairing cost absorption with transparent fixed or hourly pricing ($195–$395/hour) that avoids contingency fee conflicts of interest, ISO 31000:2009 risk governance, ISO 27001 information security controls, and a mandatory \"Six-Eye Review\" by a qualified engineer, a scientist, and a CPA or Enrolled Agent, the advisor addresses both first-year budget volatility and relational compliance anxiety. Absorbing transition friction saves a baseline corporate claimant $18,500 in Year 1 and $23,500 over five years (a 32.0% TCO reduction) while modeled client trust rises from 20% in Year 1 to 95% by Year 5, converting an initial onboarding subsidy into a high-LTV, multi-year advisory partnership."
