          "<strong>Section 174A Domestic Research Expense Test (§ 41(d)(1)(A)):</strong> The expenditures with respect to the research must be eligible to be treated as domestic <a href=\"/us/glossary/research-and-experimental-expenditures\">research or experimental expenditures</a> under IRC § 174A (meaning costs incurred in the experimental or laboratory sense to eliminate uncertainty concerning the development or improvement of a product, process, formula, invention, pilot model, or technique under Treas. Reg. § 1.174-2(a)(1)).",
          "<strong>Technological in Nature Test (§ 41(d)(1)(B)(i)):</strong> The research must be undertaken for the purpose of discovering information that is technological in nature, which under Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(a)(4) requires that the process of experimentation fundamentally rely on principles of the physical or biological sciences, engineering, or computer science.",
          "<strong>Business Component Test (§ 41(d)(1)(B)(ii)):</strong> The taxpayer must intend that the information to be discovered be useful in the development of a new or improved business component (defined in <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41d2-business-component-test\">§ 41(d)(2)(B)</a> as any product, process, computer software, technique, formula, or invention which is to be held for sale, lease, or license, or used by the taxpayer in a trade or business of the taxpayer).",
          "<strong>Process of Experimentation Test (§ 41(d)(1)(C)):</strong> Substantially all (defined in Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(a)(6) as 80 percent or more, measured on a cost or another consistently applied reasonable basis) of the research activities must constitute elements of a process of experimentation that relates to a qualified purpose under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41d3-qualified-research-permitted-purposes\">§ 41(d)(3)(A)</a>—namely, a new or improved function, performance, or reliability or quality of the business component."
