        "text": "IRC § 41(d)(4)(B) and Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(c)(3) exclude any activities relating to adapting an existing business component to a particular customer's requirement or need. If the development of a custom component for a specific customer requires resolving fundamental technological uncertainty regarding capability, method, or design through a process of experimentation under § 41(d)(1), the activity is not barred by the <a href=\"/us/glossary/adaptation-exclusion\">adaptation exclusion</a>. Conversely, modifying an existing product's dimensions, interfaces, or configuration parameters using known engineering methods to fit a customer's site specifications is excluded under § 41(d)(4)(B)."
