        "text": "Executing Section 174 and Section 174A accounting method changes while claiming Section 41 R&D credits carries substantial <a href=\"/us/faq/what-triggers-irs-rd-tax-credit-audit\">IRS audit exposure</a>. Notably, under IRS Rev. Proc. 2025-28 and IRS Rev. Proc. 2026-32, taxpayers do not receive standard Rev. Proc. 2015-13 audit protection with respect to expenditures paid or incurred in taxable years beginning before January 1, 2025, when making certain post-2024 method changes (Surgent CPE; Cherry Bekaert). Similarly, IRS Notice 2023-63 and IRS Rev. Proc. 2023-11 denied audit protection for pre-2022 taxable years and for taxpayers that failed to adopt TCJA Section 174 capitalization in their first required taxable year beginning after December 31, 2021."
