        "text": "On its Q2 2026 Form 8974 attached to Form 941, NovaBio reports the $350,000 election in Part 1, column (e) and Line 6(g) (carried to Part 2, Line 7). In Part 2, NovaBio first applies $186,000 of its $350,000 elected credit on Line 12 to offset 100% of its Q2 employer Social Security tax liability under IRC Section 3111(f)(1)(A), which falls well within the quarterly Social Security offset cap of $250,000. This leaves $164,000 of remaining credit on Line 13 ($350,000 − $186,000). Next, under the post-IRA rules expanded to Medicare tax (IRC Section 3111(f)(1)(B) and Section 3111(f)(2)), NovaBio applies $43,500 on Line 16 to offset 100% of its Q2 employer Medicare tax liability, bringing its total Q2 payroll tax credit on Form 8974, Line 17 (and Form 941, Line 11) to $229,500 and reducing its Q2 cash FICA remittance by $229,500. The unused credit balance carried forward to Q3 2026 is computed by subtracting the total Q2 offset from the initial election:"
