        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "A recurring vulnerability exposed during IRS, HMRC, and ATO examinations is reliance on retrospective narrative reconstructions drafted months or years after an engineering project has concluded. Retrospective narratives frequently suffer from survivorship bias—describing only the final commercialized design while omitting the failed iterations and rejected hypotheses that prove a process of experimentation occurred."
