    "title": "IRS Dirty Dozen list: R&D tax credit mills",
    "description": "The IRS Dirty Dozen list has repeatedly flagged abusive R&D tax credit claims and the mills that promote them under IRC § 41.",
    "summary": "The IRS Dirty Dozen list has repeatedly flagged abusive R&D tax credit claims and the mills that promote them under IRC § 41. U.S. businesses using contingency-fee or ghost-preparer promoters remain solely liable for disallowed credits, 20% accuracy-related penalties, and examinations reaching back seven or more years, so claims need contemporaneous, project-level substantiation.",
    "language": "en-US",
