        "text": "For illustrative quantification, if the baseline industry standard operating pressure is hypothetically <em>P</em><sub>std</sub> = 100 MPa, the required operational pressure threshold is <em>P</em><sub>op</sub> &gt; 1.5 × 100 MPa = 150 MPa. Second, with respect to chemical inertness, the internal wetted surfaces and metallurgical grain structure of the fitting must resist chemical degradation, intergranular stress corrosion cracking, and erosion from a specific corrosive catalyst present in the high-temperature fluid stream. Third, under the volumetric envelope constraint resulting from the miniaturized architecture of the redesigned turbine housing, the maximum allowable external volume of the coupling fitting (<em>V</em><sub>max</sub>) is restricted to 60% of the industry standard fitting volume (<em>V</em><sub>std</sub>), representing a mandatory 40% volumetric reduction:"
