        "text": "Within this diagnostic rubric, scores below 30 indicate routine engineering with low eligibility probability, scores from 30 to 59 indicate \"Potential R&D Activity - Documentation Required,\" and scores of 60 or above indicate a \"High Probability of Technical Uncertainty\". Under the baseline default configuration where <em>K</em> = 50, <em>C</em> = 50, and <em>S</em> = 50, the formula yields:"
