        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The empirical compliance data and structural governance controls evaluated in this report demonstrate that R&D tax credit audit outcomes are highly deterministic rather than random. Across the general corporate claimant population, a 44% non-compliance rate in random regulatory examinations—comprising a 25% full disallowance rate for failing statutory technical requirements and a 19% downward adjustment rate for expenditure overclaiming—exposes enterprises relying on generalist preparation to an average post-audit credit value reduction of approximately 20%."
