        "text": "Each evaluated activity is also assigned a relative matrix radius (<em>r</em>) representing its operational footprint in the analytical model. Under this framework, high placement along the horizontal <em>X</em>-axis reflects advanced clinical training, surgical precision, and anatomical complexity, whereas placement along the vertical <em>Y</em>-axis measures whether the fundamental scientific capability, method, or design is unknown and requires systematic experimentation under IRC § 41(d)(1)(C). Only activities rising above the <em>Y</em> = 50 horizontal boundary into the high-uncertainty \"Uncertainty Zone\" satisfy the statutory prerequisites for R&D tax credits."
