          "<strong>Application of the Verified IRC § 41 80% Wage Rule and Form 6765 Section G Breakdown:</strong> Because the reconstructed eligible time ratio—whether unadjusted at 65.0% (936 hours) or realism-adjusted at 55.25% (796 hours)—is below the 80% \"substantially all\" employee wage threshold under IRC § 41, the company cannot claim 100% of the three engineers' wages for the 12-week project. Instead, only the actual substantiated proportion counts. Assuming each engineer earns $3,000 per week ($36,000 per engineer over 12 weeks, or $108,000 total team payroll for the 12-week sprint), the allowable QRE wage claim under the realism-adjusted reconstruction is $108,000 × (796 ÷ 1,440) = <strong>$59,700</strong> (or $108,000 × 0.5525 = $59,670 unrounded). On revised IRS Form 6765 Section G (mandatory starting in tax year 2026 for non-exempt filers), if two of the engineers engaged in hands-on coding and testing while the third engineer acted as the first-line supervisor directing the experimental design, the $59,700 QRE figure for that business component must be disaggregated on Section G into <strong>$39,800 of Direct Research Wages</strong> and <strong>$19,900 of Direct Supervision Wages</strong>."
