        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "While a structured expert interview anchored to Evidence-Based Timelines (EBTR) and vetted through a multi-disciplinary Six-Eye Review provides a defensible mechanism for past periods where hours were not tracked, retrospective reconstruction requires substantial forensic effort and faces higher audit scrutiny than <a href=\"/us/glossary/contemporaneous-documentation\">contemporaneous record-keeping</a>. Based on verified guidance from the IRS, ATO, HMRC, and specialist compliance practitioners, organizations should implement a two-stage transition strategy."
