        "text": "Strategic tax-modeling consideration: Because electing to deduct the remaining 90% of 2024 domestic R&E costs (along with the remaining 70% of 2023 costs and 50% of 2022 costs) either entirely in 2025 or ratably across 2025 and 2026 substantially reduces taxable income in those years, taxpayers must evaluate collateral interactions with taxable-income-sensitive provisions—such as the Section 163(j) business interest expense limitation, the Section 250 foreign-derived deduction eligible income (FDDEI) deduction, net operating loss (NOL) 80% absorption limits under Section 172, and Base Erosion and Anti-Abuse Tax (BEAT) thresholds under Section 59A—before selecting between the 1-year acceleration, the 2-year ratable acceleration, or continuing the 5-year TCJA schedule."
