          "<strong>Statutory deadline:</strong> Under § 70302(f)(1)(B) of Pub. L. 119-21, the retroactive election had to be made within one year of the date of enactment (July 4, 2025). Because July 4, 2026, fell on a Saturday (and was a legal holiday), Rev. Proc. 2025-28 sections 2.06(2) and 3.03(3) established the final deadline (pursuant to IRC Section 7503) as <strong>Monday, July 6, 2026</strong>, or, if earlier with respect to a specific prior taxable year, the expiration of the period of limitations for filing a claim for credit or refund under IRC Section 6511(a) for that taxable year. <em>Note: As of November 11, 2026, the July 6, 2026 deadline for small business retroactive amended-return elections under § 70302(f)(1) has expired.</em>",
          "<strong>Procedural mechanics (Amended Returns, AARs, or Accounting Method Change):</strong> Under section 3.03(2) of Rev. Proc. 2025-28, an eligible small business making the retroactive election via return filings was required to attach a statement titled \"FILED PURSUANT TO SECTION 3.03 OF REV. PROC. 2025-28\" to its original return, amended return (e.g., Form 1120-X or Form 1040-X), or partnership Administrative Adjustment Request (AAR under IRC Section 6227) for each applicable taxable year. Under section 3.03(4), an original return for an applicable taxable year (such as an extended 2024 return) timely filed on or before November 15, 2025, that deducted domestic research or experimental expenditures was deemed to have validly made the § 70302(f)(1) election for that year without the formal statement, provided the taxpayer timely filed amended returns or AARs for its earlier 2022 and 2023 applicable years. Alternatively, rather than filing multiple amended returns or AARs for 2022–2024, Rev. Proc. 2025-28 section 7 (modifying section 7.02(3)(c) of Rev. Proc. 2025-23) permitted an eligible small business to implement the retroactive § 70302(f)(1) election as an automatic change in method of accounting on its 2024 or 2025 return using a modified IRC Section 481(a) adjustment (provided the change was made in connection with a timely § 70302(f)(1) election by July 6, 2026).",
