        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Under IRC Section 41(d)(1) (as amended by Pub. L. 119-21, § 70302(d) to reference Section 174A), research activities constitute \"qualified research\" eligible for the federal Research and Development (R&D) tax credit only if four cumulative statutory requirements (commonly known as the <a href=\"/us/faq/rd-tax-credit-four-part-test-explained\">Four-Part Test</a>, detailed in Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(a)) are satisfied with respect to each separate business component:"
