        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "To prevent taxpayers from claiming both a full tax deduction (or full capital basis recovery) and a full tax credit on the exact same dollar of research expenditure, IRC Section 280C(c) requires coordination between <a href=\"/us/faq/section-41-credit-vs-section-174-expenses\">Section 174/174A and the Section 41 research credit</a>. During the 2022–2024 TCJA window, <a href=\"/us/faq/does-rd-tax-credit-reduce-tax-basis-section-280c\">former Section 280C(c)(1)</a> contained a modified rule providing that the capitalized amount under Section 174 was reduced only to the extent that the Section 41(a) research credit exceeded the amount allowable as an amortization deduction for that taxable year."
