        "text": "As the five-year projection demonstrates, optimizing technical substantiation to achieve an 85% eligibility capture rate yields $119,000 in Year 1 and $726,507 in cumulative five-year tax benefits, compared to $70,000 in Year 1 and $427,357 over five years under a conservative 50% capture rate—generating an additional $299,150 in non-dilutive capital available for talent acquisition and technology reinvestment. (Note that under the statutory ASC calculation of <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41c4-alternative-simplified-credit\">IRC § 41(c)(4)(A)</a>, the 14% rate applies to current-year QREs exceeding 50% of the average QREs for the three preceding taxable years, or 6% of current-year QREs under IRC § 41(c)(4)(B) if the taxpayer had no QREs in any one of the three preceding taxable years, while the model above isolates the gross 14% statutory rate multiplier on incremental/captured spend)."
