        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "A disallowance triggers 100% principal recapture (or refund freeze and rejection), compounding statutory underpayment interest running from the unextended original return due date under 26 U.S.C. § 6601(a) and (b)(1), a 20% civil penalty under either 26 U.S.C. § 6676(a) (for excessive refund or credit claims) or 26 U.S.C. § 6662(a) (for tax underpayments attributable to negligence or substantial understatement of income tax), and tens of thousands of dollars in external specialist defense fees ($195 to $395 per hour) alongside severe internal engineering distraction."
