          "<strong>Example 6 (Passenger Rail Car Adaptation):</strong> Illustrates the adaptation exclusion under IRC § 41(d)(4)(B) and 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(3) in manufacturing, where rail car manufacturer X fulfills an order from customer B for passenger rail cars differing from existing models solely by having fewer seats and commercially available upgraded seating material and carpet.",
