          "<strong>Example 8 (Duplication Versus Alternative Formulation Experimentation):</strong> Illustrates the <a href=\"/us/glossary/duplication-exclusion\">duplication exclusion</a> under IRC § 41(d)(4)(C) and 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(4) (and is cited by the IRS Software PoE Audit Guidelines against reverse engineering), where X analyzes and reproduces ingredients A and B of competitor Y's gasoline additive (excluded duplication), but then conducts a qualifying process of experimentation to develop and test alternative lower-cost replacements for ingredient C (not excluded as duplication).",
