        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "At the same time, existing Treasury regulations and judicial precedent already provide a coherent analytical path: customer specificity does not disqualify a project <em>per se</em> under 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(3), and taxpayers who maintain granular, subcomponent-level documentation of their upfront design uncertainties, alternative evaluations, and 80% experimentation allocation can substantiate custom development work under 26 CFR § 1.41-4(a)(5)–(6) and (b)(2)."
