          "<strong>Supplies Used in Qualified Research (26 U.S.C. § 41(b)(2)(A)(ii), (C); Form 6765, Line 43):</strong> Any amount paid or incurred for supplies used in the conduct of qualified research. Under § 41(b)(2)(C), the term \"supplies\" means any tangible property other than (i) land or improvements to land, and (ii) property of a character subject to the allowance for depreciation. Depreciation allowances themselves and capital equipment purchases are <a href=\"/us/faq/excluded-expenses-rd-tax-credit\">excluded from § 41 QREs</a> even when the equipment is used exclusively in R&D.",
          "<strong>Right to Use Computers (26 U.S.C. § 41(b)(2)(A)(iii); Form 6765, Line 44):</strong> Under regulations prescribed by the Secretary, any amount paid or incurred to another person for the right to use (<a href=\"/us/faq/aws-cloud-hosting-costs-rd-tax-credit\">rental or lease of off-premises or cloud</a>) computers in the conduct of qualified research. Under the flush language of § 41(b)(2)(A), this clause does not apply to any amount to the extent that the taxpayer (or any person with whom the taxpayer must aggregate expenditures under § 41(f)(1)) receives or accrues any amount from any other person for the right to use substantially identical personal property.",
          "<strong>Contract Research Expenses (<a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41b3-contract-research-expenses\">26 U.S.C. § 41(b)(3)</a>; Form 6765, Lines 45–47):</strong> Generally, under § 41(b)(3)(A), <a href=\"/us/faq/contractor-expenses-65-percent-rule-rd-credit\">65% of any amount paid or incurred</a> by the taxpayer to any person (other than an employee of the taxpayer) for qualified research. The statutory inclusion rate increases to 75% under § 41(b)(3)(C) for amounts paid or incurred to a \"qualified research consortium\"—defined as any organization described in IRC § 501(c)(3) or § 501(c)(6) that is exempt from tax under § 501(a), is organized and operated primarily to conduct scientific research, and is not a private foundation—for qualified research conducted on behalf of the taxpayer and one or more unrelated taxpayers (treating all persons aggregated under IRC § 52(a) or (b) as related). Furthermore, the statutory inclusion rate increases to 100% under § 41(b)(3)(D) for amounts paid by the taxpayer to (I) an eligible small business (a business with 500 or fewer average annual employees during either of the 2 preceding calendar years in which the taxpayer owns less than 50% of the voting/value stock or capital/profits interests under IRC § 318), (II) an institution of higher education (as defined in 26 U.S.C. § 3304(f)), or (III) a Federal laboratory (as defined in § 4(6) of the Stevenson-Wydler Technology Innovation Act of 1980, 15 U.S.C. § 3703(6)), for qualified research which is energy research. Under § 41(b)(3)(B), if any contract research expenses paid or incurred during any taxable year are attributable to qualified research to be conducted after the close of such taxable year, such prepaid amounts are treated as paid or incurred only during the subsequent period in which the qualified research is actually conducted."
