        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "As the calculation demonstrates, in Scenario A, where the four-year AAGR is $8,000,000, the unfloored Traditional base ($800,000) is below the 50% minimum floor ($1,000,000), yielding an unreduced Traditional Credit of $200,000 that outperforms the ASC ($175,000) by $25,000. However, in Scenario B, doubling the company's four-year AAGR from $8,000,000 to $16,000,000 drives the unfloored Traditional base to $1,600,000, slashing the unreduced Traditional Credit by 60% (from $200,000 down to $80,000), whereas the unreduced ASC remains constant at $175,000 ($95,000 higher than the Traditional Credit in Scenario B) because the ASC formula is completely insulated from gross receipts growth."
