        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "In evaluating start-up eligibility for the Fixed-Base Percentage under the RRC, tax practitioners must avoid conflating the <a href=\"/us/glossary/qualified-small-business-qsb\">Qualified Small Business (QSB)</a> eligibility test for the payroll tax credit election under IRC § 41(h)(3) with the \"start-up company\" definition under IRC § 41(c)(3)(B). Whereas IRC § 41(h)(3) requires a QSB to have less than $5,000,000 in gross receipts for the credit year and no gross receipts prior to the five-tax-year period ending with the credit year, those revenue thresholds have no bearing on the 3% Fixed-Base Percentage under the RRC."
