        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Second, under 26 CFR § 1.41-3(b)(1), if the current credit year itself is a short taxable year, the Base Amount determined under IRC § 41(c)(1) (or, equivalently as framed in the IRS ATG, the four-year AAGR used in § 41(c)(1))—but never the 50% minimum base amount under § 41(c)(2)—is prorated downward by multiplying by the number of months in the short credit year and dividing by 12:"
