        "text": "The strategic <a href=\"/us/faq/asc-vs-regular-rd-tax-credit-method\">selection between the RRC and ASC</a> Base Amount methodologies turns on the underlying financial variables driving each threshold. Under the RRC, because the Base Amount equals FBP × AAGR, rapid expansion in a taxpayer's top-line gross receipts over the four preceding years automatically inflates the Base Amount, even when the company's R&D budget has grown steadily in absolute terms. When revenue expands at a faster rate than QREs, the RRC Base Amount can overtake current-year QREs and extinguish the regular credit entirely, imposing a severe growth penalty on rapidly scaling enterprises."
