        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Conversely, because the ASC Base Amount is 50% of the rolling three-year QRE average (or 1/6 of the three-year QRE sum), it is completely insulated from top-line revenue surges. However, the ASC Base Amount exhibits heightened sensitivity to QRE volatility. A sharp, one-time surge in QREs in Year t immediately enters the three-year look-back average for Years t + 1, t + 2, and t + 3, elevating the ASC Base Amount by 1/6 (16.67%) of that expenditure spike in each of the subsequent three years. If research expenditures moderate to baseline levels after a major capital or development project concludes, the inflated rolling average can substantially compress or eliminate the ASC benefit across the following three-year cycle."
