        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "For non-corporate trades or businesses under common control governed by IRC § 41(f)(1)(B) and § 52(b), Treas. Reg. § 1.41-6(a)(3)(ii) and (v) align the definitions of \"controlled group\" and \"trade or business\" with IRC § 52(b) and Treas. Reg. § 1.52-1(b) through (g), encompassing sole proprietorships, partnerships, LLCs, trusts, estates, and corporations that stand under common control. This statutory extension ensures that <a href=\"/us/glossary/pass-through-entity-rd-credit\">pass-through entities</a>, fiduciaries, and unincorporated businesses cannot structure their operations across non-corporate legal forms to bypass mandatory aggregation."
