        "type": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "<strong>Regulatory Promulgation Date:</strong> Treas. Reg. § 1.41-2(b)(4) was promulgated on May 17, 1989, under Treasury Decision (T.D.) 8251 (54 FR 21204; subsequently amended by T.D. 8930, 65 FR 287, Jan. 3, 2001), not in 1985; the 1985 reference reflects the post-December 31, 1985 statutory effective date established by the Tax Reform Act of 1986 (Public Law 99-514).",
          "<strong>Statutory Reduction Clause and \"Substantially All\" Contradiction:</strong> The flush language of IRC § 41(b)(2)(A)(iii) contains a mandatory reduction clause disqualifying computer rental payments to the extent the taxpayer (or any person with whom the taxpayer must aggregate expenditures under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41f-rd-tax-credit-special-rules\">IRC § 41(f)(1)</a>) receives or accrues any amount from any other person for the right to use substantially identical personal property.",
          "<strong>Contract Research Inclusion Tiers:</strong> While the general inclusion rate for contract research expenses is 65% under IRC § 41(b)(3)(A) and Treas. Reg. § 1.41-2(e)(1), the statute provides a 75% inclusion rate for amounts paid to qualified research consortia under IRC § 41(b)(3)(C) and a 100% inclusion rate for eligible energy research payments made to eligible small businesses, universities, or federal laboratories under IRC § 41(b)(3)(D).",
          "<strong>Form 6765 Section G Effective Dates, Exemptions, and Narrative Rules:</strong> Itemized business component reporting on Form 6765, Section G (where computer rental costs are reported on Line/Column 55 and summed on Section F, Line 44) is optional for all filers for tax years beginning before 2026 and becomes mandatory only for tax years beginning after 2025. Even for tax years beginning after 2025, exemptions apply to <a href=\"/us/glossary/qualified-small-business-qsb\">Qualified Small Businesses (QSBs)</a> electing the reduced payroll tax credit under IRC § 41(h) and to taxpayers claiming the credit on an original return with total controlled-group QREs equal to or less than $1.5 million and prior three-year average annual gross receipts equal to or less than $50 million. Moreover, narrative descriptions of the information sought to be discovered in Section G, Column 49(f) are required only on amended returns claiming a new or increased research credit, not on timely filed original returns.",
          "<strong>Scope of the 2025 Final Cloud Regulations (T.D. 10022):</strong> Final regulations published on January 14, 2025 (T.D. 10022, 90 FR 2977; Treas. Reg. §§ 1.861-18 and 1.861-19) classify all cloud transactions (IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS) solely as the provision of services rather than leases of property, but Section VI of the preamble explicitly restricts this classification to enumerated international tax provisions of the Code. Through Notice 2025-6 (2025-8 I.R.B. 799), Treasury and the IRS are evaluating whether to extend Treas. Reg. §§ 1.861-18 and 1.861-19 across all provisions of the Internal Revenue Code—a step that, without a concurrent IRC § 41 carve-out or regulatory update, could conflict with treating cloud computing as a 100% in-house computer rental expense."
        ]
