        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Qualified wages paid or incurred to an employee for qualified services under IRC § 41(b)(2)(A)(i) and § 41(b)(2)(B) (consisting of engaging in qualified research, or engaging in the <a href=\"/us/glossary/direct-supervision\">direct supervision</a> or direct support of qualified research) constitute the largest dollar component of most R&D tax credit claims and represent the single most frequent point of failure under the Consistency Rule during IRS audits. <a href=\"/us/faq/signs-of-aggressive-rd-tax-credit-advisor\">Aggressive credit studies</a> prepared by third-party consultants frequently employ a \"blanket approach,\" assigning high allocation percentages—sometimes 100 percent of wages under the \"<a href=\"/us/glossary/substantially-all-rule\">substantially all</a>\" (80 percent) wage rule of IRC § 41(b)(2)(B) and Treas. Reg. § 1.41-2(d)(2)—to employee categories that historically performed routine operations or production support."
