        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The Consistency Rule applies with equal force to non-wage QREs under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41b1-qualified-research-expenses\">IRC § 41(b)</a>. For contract research expenses (CRE) under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41b3-contract-research-expenses\">IRC § 41(b)(3)(A)</a>, where a taxpayer generally claims 65 percent of amounts paid or incurred to any person (other than an employee of the taxpayer) for qualified research (or 75 percent for payments to a qualified research consortium under § 41(b)(3)(C), and 100 percent for eligible energy research payments under § 41(b)(3)(D)), the exact same statutory percentage limitation and qualification criteria must be applied to all comparable third-party research payments during the 1984–1988 base years. Likewise, under IRC § 41(b)(2)(A)(iii) and Treas. Reg. § 1.41-2(b)(4), amounts paid or incurred to another person for the right to use (time-sharing) computers in the conduct of qualified research—increasingly claimed for modern cloud-computing development environments—require consistent inclusion of historical mainframe or computer time-sharing expenses incurred during the 1984–1988 base period."
