        "text": "Structural corporate transformations—including mergers, acquisitions, spin-offs, and dispositions of a major portion of a trade or business (or a separate unit thereof) under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41f-rd-tax-credit-special-rules\">IRC § 41(f)(3)(A)–(B)</a>—compound the complexity of maintaining historical consistency across predecessor entities. Acquiring or divesting a business unit requires integrating or carving out 1984–1988 base-period QREs and gross receipts from predecessor accounting systems so that the post-transaction taxpayer's FBP and four-year AAGR reflect the exact scope of trades or businesses present in the credit year. Similarly, under IRC § 41(f)(1) and Treas. Reg. § 1.41-6, all members of a <a href=\"/us/glossary/controlled-group\">controlled group of corporations</a> or trades or businesses under common control are treated as a single taxpayer, requiring aggregated and consistent base-period data across all group members."
