        "text": "First, <em>Deere & Co. v. Commissioner</em>, 133 T.C. 246 (133 T.C. No. 11, Oct. 22, 2009), did not involve ships or base-period QRE asset exclusions; rather, it adjudicated the <strong>gross receipts</strong> component of the Regular Credit base amount calculation under IRC § 41(c). In <em>Deere & Co.</em>, the taxpayer omitted the annual gross receipts of its foreign branches (overseas divisions) when computing its average annual gross receipts for the four preceding taxable years under IRC § 41(c)(1)(B). The Tax Court denied the claimed research credits, holding that Congress did not exclude foreign branch receipts of a domestic corporation from the gross receipts calculation under IRC § 41(c)."
