        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The federal tax compliance landscape governing the IRC § 41 Research and Development Tax Credit has undergone an irreversible structural transformation. For decades, many taxpayers treated R&D substantiation as a retrospective exercise—filing aggregate computational numbers on Form 6765 and relying on post-hoc manager interviews or departmental percentage estimates to reconstruct project narratives only if selected for audit. The confluence of the IRS Research Credit Claims Audit Techniques Guide's enforcement against the \"hybrid/nexus problem,\" judicial hostility toward uncorroborated allocations under <em>United States v. McFerrin</em>, the stringent refund claim specificity rules of CCA 20214101F, and the mandatory business-component disaggregation of modernized Form 6765 Sections E and G has rendered retrospective estimation obsolete."
