        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "By contrast, for Employee B, an Engineering Manager earning $160,000 across 2,000 annual hours, the claim relies on an uncorroborated flat estimate patterned after Scenario A and <em>Phoenix Design Group</em>. Without referencing specific business components, version-control logs, or design specifications, Employee B offers a generalized assertion that \"about 40% of time (800 hours out of 2,000 annual hours, or $64,000 in claimed wages) was spent on complicated R&D work\". Because this testimony fails to identify a technical uncertainty under IRC § 174, lacks nexus to any defined business component under IRC § 41(d)(2)(B), provides zero factual support for the 40% assumption, and conflicts with contemporaneous project records showing routine compliance tasks, the entire $64,000 wage claim is disallowed ($0.00 allowed QREs) under the IRS ATG and <em>Phoenix Design Group</em>."
