        "text": "Taken together, the three prongs of the HTIT under 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vii) function as a deliberate regulatory firewall. By requiring a \"higher level of uncertainty and technical risk than that required for business components that are not internal use software\" under 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vii)(C) and conditioning commercial unavailability on modifications that independently satisfy both the substantial cost/speed improvement test and the heightened economic risk test under 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vii)(A)(3), Treasury regulations systematically screen out conventional enterprise IT modernization projects."
