        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "This quantitative breakdown demonstrates a critical second-order financial reality of ERP tax credit planning: because external systems integration consultants suffer a 35% statutory haircut under IRC Section 41(b)(3)(A) whereas internal technical wages are 100% eligible under IRC Section 41(b)(2), deploying internal software engineers on the most technically uncertain custom integration modules yields a 53.8% higher QRE recovery per dollar spent than outsourcing that identical experimental work to <a href=\"/us/faq/outsourced-contractor-rd-tax-credit-eligibility\">third-party contractors</a> (1.00 / 0.65 = 1.538)."
