        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "In <strong>Hypothetical Scenario 1 (Example 13 — Safe Harbor Inapplicable Due to &lt;10% Anticipated Third-Party Use)</strong>, X develops Dual Function Software costing $50,000 and is unable to identify a discrete third-party subset under § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vi)(B). Using an objective, reasonable method at the beginning of development, X determines that third-party use to initiate functions is reasonably anticipated to constitute 5% of the software's total use. Because 5% is less than the minimum 10% usage threshold of 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vi)(C), safe harbor QRE recovery is $0 (0% × $50,000 = $0). The entire $50,000 is presumed to be IUS under § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vi)(A) and can be included in computing the research credit only if the software satisfies all three prongs of the HTI test under § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vii)."
