          "<strong>Contemporaneous Intent Documentation (26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(6)(v)) (Phase I):</strong> Preserve inception-date project charters, product roadmaps, architectural specifications, and capital authorization requests demonstrating initial project purpose, because classification as IUS, Non-IUS, or DFS depends on the taxpayer's intent and the facts and circumstances at the beginning of software development (§ 1.41-4(c)(6)(v) and (vi)(D)), and segregate any subsequent software improvements into separate business components evaluated according to their own inception-date intent.",
