    "title": "Notice of Claim Disallowance",
    "description": "A Notice of Claim Disallowance (IRS Letter 105C or 106C) is the IRS's final rejection of a refund claim and starts a two-year deadline to sue.",
    "summary": "A Notice of Claim Disallowance (IRS Letter 105C for a full denial or Letter 106C for a partial denial) is the IRS's final rejection of a U.S. refund claim, including R&D tax credits under IRC § 41. Its certified mailing starts a two-year deadline under IRC § 6532(a)(1) to sue in federal court; Appeals review does not pause it.",
    "language": "en-US",
