    "summary": "Routine data collection is a categorical exclusion from the U.S. federal R&D tax credit under IRC Section 41(d)(4)(D)(iv). It bars taxpayers from treating operational monitoring, standard fact-finding, or non-investigatory measurement as qualified research, so wages, supplies, and contractor costs tied to it must be segregated and excluded from qualified research expenses.",
