        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Whether a technical data-gathering activity falls into the categorical exclusion of IRC § 41(d)(4)(D)(iv) or qualifies as experimental data acquisition under IRC § 41(d)(1)(C) depends on the objective technological uncertainty present at the outset of the activity and the evaluative methodology employed, rather than the physical sensor, laboratory instrument, or software logging tool used to capture the data. The table below synthesizes the statutory, regulatory, and judicial boundaries across excluded RDC, adjacent survey and quality-control exclusions, and qualified experimental data acquisition."
