        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "To illustrate the exact quantitative mechanics of the three-tier waterfall under Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vi)(A)–(C), consider the worked compliance scenario involving a corporate taxpayer that incurs <strong>$1,000,000</strong> in total domestic software engineering wages and cloud development environment costs during the taxable year to engineer a hybrid enterprise fulfillment and financial settlement platform, where all software modules satisfy the standard four-part test of IRC § 41(d)(1) (alongside the scaled <strong>$10,000,000</strong> enterprise portfolio variant)."
