        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "When software is developed primarily for internal use in a G&A function (financial management, human resources management, or day-to-day support services) under Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(c)(6)(iii) and is not covered by the commercial, operational, research/production process, integral hardware-software, or dual-function safe-harbor pathways, it can qualify as Specially Designed Software under Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(c)(6)(i)(C) only by satisfying all three cumulative prongs of the <strong><a href=\"/us/glossary/high-threshold-of-innovation-test\">High Threshold of Innovation (HTI) Test</a></strong> codified at Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vii). Just as with initial IUS classification, Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vii)(D) mandates that the HTI test takes into account only the results anticipated to be attributable to the development of new or improved software at the <strong>beginning of the software development</strong>."
