        "text": "The third prong of the HTI test—codified at Treas. Reg. § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vii)(A)(3)—mandates that the software is <a href=\"/us/glossary/commercial-availability-standard\">not commercially available</a> for use by the taxpayer at the beginning of the development project, in that the software cannot be purchased, leased, or licensed and used for the taxpayer's intended purpose without requiring modifications that would, in and of themselves, satisfy both the Innovativeness requirement of paragraph (c)(6)(vii)(A)(1) and the Significant Economic Risk requirement of paragraph (c)(6)(vii)(A)(2)."
