        "text": "This requirement forecloses R&D tax credit claims for standard implementations of commercial off-the-shelf (COTS) enterprise packages. When a taxpayer licenses an <a href=\"/us/glossary/erp-implementation-qualification\">enterprise resource planning (ERP)</a>, customer relationship management (CRM), or human capital management (HCM) suite, routine configuration, workflow mapping, user-interface localization, and standard API integration do not satisfy Criterion 3. Only where commercial software is fundamentally incapable of performing the required function—necessitating custom architectural extensions or bespoke algorithmic modules that independently face substantial technical risk of non-recovery—can the modification costs qualify under the HTI framework."
