        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "One of the most economically punitive provisions of the amended Section 174 regime is IRC Section 174(d), which governs the disposition, retirement, or abandonment of property connected to capitalized research expenditures. Under TCJA IRC Section 174(d) and Section 7.02 of IRS Notice 2023-63, if any property with respect to which SRE expenditures were paid or incurred is disposed of, retired, or abandoned during the applicable 5-year or 15-year amortization period, no deduction or loss recovery is allowed on account of such disposition, retirement, or abandonment; instead, such amortization must continue with respect to such expenditures over the remainder of the original statutory period. Under Section 7.03 of Notice 2023-63, this prohibition applies even when the underlying property is disposed of, retired, or abandoned prior to the midpoint of the taxable year in which the SRE expenditures were initially paid or incurred."
