          "<strong>Tax Years 2022–2024 (<a href=\"/us/glossary/tax-cuts-and-jobs-act-tcja\">TCJA</a> Capitalization Regime):</strong> Under the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017 (TCJA, P.L. 115-97), effective for taxable years beginning after December 31, 2021, through taxable years beginning before January 1, 2025, Congress amended 26 U.S.C. § 174 to eliminate immediate expensing and mandate that \"<a href=\"/us/glossary/specified-research-or-experimental-expenditures-sre\">specified research or experimental expenditures</a>\" be capitalized and amortized ratably over 5 years for domestic research and 15 years for foreign research, while amending 26 U.S.C. § 41(d)(1)(A) to reference expenditures that <em>\"may be treated as specified research or experimental expenditures under section 174\"</em>.",
