        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Under 26 C.F.R. § 1.41-4(a)(6), the ≥80% Process of Experimentation threshold is measured \"on a cost or other consistently applied reasonable basis (and without regard to section 1.41-2(d)(2))\". In examination practice, defending the 26 C.F.R. § 1.41-4(a)(6) calculation on a cost basis is substantially more complex than defending the hourly employee wage fraction under 26 C.F.R. § 1.41-2(d), because taxpayers must establish a <a href=\"/us/glossary/project-to-expense-nexus\">documented nexus</a> allocating labor and third-party contract research activities between active Process of Experimentation tasks and non-evaluative tasks at the individual business component level. Two major measurement fallacies have been decisively rejected by the U.S. Tax Court in <em>Little Sandy Coal Co., Inc. v. Commissioner</em>, T.C. Memo. 2021-15 (affirmed on appeal, 62 F.4th 287 (7th Cir. 2023))."
