    "summary": "The Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (TCJA) of 2017 required U.S. businesses to capitalize research and experimental expenditures under IRC Section 174, amortizing domestic costs over five years and foreign costs over 15 years starting in 2022. This shift outweighed Section 41 R&D credit benefits until the OBBBA's Section 174A restored domestic expensing from 2025.",
