        "text": "In evaluating the legislative remedies to mandatory Section 174 amortization, an explicit clarification of statutory chronology is essential. While compliance guidance written from a 2024 tax-year vantage point framed the One Big Beautiful Bill Act (OBBBA) as proposed legislation while emphasizing <a href=\"/us/faq/section-174-amortization-changes-2024\">mandatory capitalization for 2024 returns</a>, the enacted July 2025 OBBBA statutory framework formally established IRC Section 174A. Accordingly, comprehensive tax analysis must preserve both the strict Section 174 capitalization compliance requirements governing the 2022 through 2024 baseline tax years and the post-2024 transition and prospective expensing rules instituted under the enacted OBBBA."
