          "<strong>Terminological Conflation with Outsourced \"Funded Research\" (26 CFR § 1.41-4A(d)):</strong> In federal tax law, \"third party subset\" is exclusively a term of art under 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(6)(vi)(B) for external-facing elements of dual-function software; research performed by or for outside contractors is governed separately by the <a href=\"/us/glossary/funded-research\">Funded Research exclusion</a> (IRC § 41(d)(4)(H), 26 CFR § 1.41-4(c)(9), and 26 CFR § 1.41-4A(d)) and the Contract Research Expense rules (IRC § 41(b)(3) and 26 CFR § 1.41-2(e)).",
          "<strong>Omission of the Mandatory 10% Third-Party Use Threshold for the 25% Safe Harbor:</strong> To claim the 25% safe harbor, the taxpayer must determine at the beginning of software development, using an objective, reasonable method within the taxpayer's industry (such as processing time, amount of data transfer, or number of software user interface screens), that third-party use of the dual-function software or dual-function subset (or use by the taxpayer to interact with third parties) is reasonably anticipated to constitute at least 10 percent of total use.",
