          "<strong>Contractual Alignment with the \"Mirror-Image\" Risk Rules:</strong> Before claiming <a href=\"/us/faq/contractor-expenses-65-percent-rule-rd-credit\">65% contract research expenses</a> as a payer under 26 CFR § 1.41-2(e)(2), the taxpayer must verify that the prior agreement obligates the payer to bear the cost even if the research fails; conversely, when performing contracted engineering or development for clients, the taxpayer must ensure that payment is contingent on technical success (backed by express rejection/remedy clauses) and that it retains non-exclusive rights to use the underlying research know-how under 26 CFR § 1.41-4A(d) (<em>Fairchild Industries</em>, <em>Lockheed Martin</em>, <em>Populous Holdings</em>, <em>Dynetics</em>, and <em>Meyer, Borgman & Johnson</em>).",
