          "<strong>Indiana Case Law Conflation (<em>Tell City Boatworks</em> vs. <em>System Technologies</em>):</strong> In fact, in <em>Tell City Boatworks, Inc. v. Indiana Department of State Revenue</em>, 162 N.E.3d 603 (Ind. Tax Ct. 2020), the Indiana Tax Court denied the Indiana research credit because the taxpayer failed the business component test under IRC § 41(d)(1)(B)(ii) and <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41d2-business-component-test\">§ 41(d)(2)(B)</a> on Project 112 and failed the 80% process-of-experimentation test on Projects 107, 109, and 111. The ruling that Indiana contract law refund remedies prevented customer purchase orders from constituting \"funded research\" under IRC § 41(d)(4)(H) was issued by the U.S. Tax Court in <em>System Technologies, Inc. v. Commissioner</em>, Docket No. 12211-21 (Order dated January 3, 2025).",
