        "text": "The third exhaustive category of in-house research expenses under 26 U.S.C. § 41(b)(2)(A)(iii) consists of, \"under regulations prescribed by the Secretary, any amount paid or incurred to another person for the right to use computers in the conduct of qualified research\". Originally enacted when companies leased time-sharing processing capacity on off-site mainframe supercomputers, this provision now serves as the statutory basis for claiming third-party <a href=\"/us/faq/aws-cloud-hosting-costs-rd-tax-credit\">cloud computing infrastructure costs</a>—such as Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform (GCP)—incurred for software compilation, load-testing simulations, sandbox virtual machines, and artificial intelligence or machine learning model training."
