        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Thus, as CRS Report RL31181 confirms, whenever a taxpayer's current-year research intensity (the ratio of current-year QREs to prior four-year average annual gross receipts) is more than double its historical fixed-base percentage (or exceeds 32 percent of prior four-year AAGR for a firm at the 16 percent FBP cap), the taxpayer is automatically bound by the 50 percent minimum base amount floor of § 41(c)(2)."
