        "text": "In <strong>Phase 2 (State Applications: Georgia vs. California)</strong>, AeroCode AI LLC's state-apportioned QREs yield starkly different liquidity outcomes. In Georgia, applying the 10 percent statutory rate under O.C.G.A. § 48-7-40.12 to $1,000,000 of Georgia QREs minus the $300,000 startup base amount (30% × $1,000,000 Georgia gross receipts) produces a <strong>$70,000</strong> Georgia R&D credit:"
